# WHAT EACH ABSORBING BUFFER WAS ASKED TO HOLD, BESIDE HOW MUCH IT HOLDS. One row per
# (interfering layer, buffer it named) carrying the shares attributed to that buffer and the
# slack filed for it.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE UNSERVED HOLDERS ARE EXEMPT AND THAT EXEMPTION IS THE ARGUMENT, NOT A
#    TECHNICALITY. The remaining holders name somebody who ABSORBED the remainder, so their
#    shares have to fit inside the buffer that did the absorbing. `customer` and `unrealised`
#    name demand that was never met by anyone -- it is the overflow, not a load on the
#    buffer, so counting it would bound the wrong quantity.
#
# ✅⭐⭐⭐ THE EXEMPTION IS AN ANTI-JOIN NOW, NOT A KIND LIST. It read `kind <> 'unrealised'`,
#    which exempted one member of a class of two and summed `customer` -- demand that was
#    MADE and went unserved -- into the buffer's load. checks/clearance_with_unserved.sqlc
#    ranges over the complement of this population and calls that same PAIR a violation, and
#    entries/unserved_holders.sqlc is where the pair is named. Three partitions of five kinds
#    lived here; there is one definition between them now, and it is in one file.
#
# ⛔⛔ INTERFERENCE ONLY, WHERE `pressed` ALSO ADMITS `transition`, AND THAT NARROWING IS THE
#    REPAIR. Under a transition the holder shares carry the CLEARANCE magnitude -- `|n - d|`
#    is the larger side and it is what the filer can count -- while the buffer slack bounds
#    the INTERFERENCE side. The inequality then compares opposite edges of one buffer.
#    `Fit` says the two sides are anticorrelated and must be evaluated AT A CORNER, and
#    nothing in this relation can pick one. checks/exposure_unaccounted.sqlc is the rule
#    written for that case: it reaches the same layers through the implied exposure instead,
#    and suspends rather than passing when the unserved share is unstated.
#
# ⛔ HOLDER IS INCIDENCE, NOT ABSORPTION -- the words are the XSD's, in the section header
#   above `HolderKind`. Which holders absorbed is not a fact the type carries. It is read
#   here from the sign and the unserved class, and that reading belongs to this file rather
#   than to any filing.
#
# ⛔ ONLY A SIZED SLACK BOUNDS ANYTHING. A buffer filed `unmeasured` has no magnitude to
#   compare against, so those rows are absent rather than passing -- a bound with nothing to
#   bound passes loudest.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THE BUFFER IS REACHED THROUGH A READER'S ASSERTION. The absorber is a borrowed
#    term; deciding that it names one of the three structural buffers is a judgement recorded
#    in layers/absorber.sqlc, not a fact any filing states.
# ⛔⛔⛔ THE ANTI-JOIN IS WHY `share_exceeds_slack` READS ⛔ VACUOUS, AND THE VACUUM IS A FINDING
#    ABOUT THE EVIDENCE RATHER THAN A GAP IN IT. Traced stage by stage: 23 pressed layers, all 23
#    keep their absorber and their holders, 4 survive `slack is SIZED`, 3 survive
#    `sign = interference` -- and the anti-join then removes all three.
#
#    ⭐ It removes them because **every holder on all three is `customer` or `unrealised`**:
#    `enterprise-contract/capability` and `contrato-empresarial/capacidade-entregavel` (2 + 1
#    each) and `merge-holding-composition/shift-line` (1.7 + 1.0). Six holders, six unserved.
#    So on every interference layer in this corpus that sizes its absorbing buffer, NOTHING WAS
#    ABSORBED AT ALL -- the demand was turned away. `Σ served shares ≤ S` has an empty left side
#    because no share was served, which is the model's own subject stated by the data.
#
#    ⛔ Disable the anti-join and three rows appear: 2.7, 3 and 3 against slacks of their own.
#    That is not the rule waking up; it is the rule counting turned-away demand as absorbed.
#
# ⚠️ AND PROBE IT RATHER THAN READING THE ZERO. A `0` here is produced by a working anti-join, by
#   a broken one, and by an upstream filter that emptied the population -- three different facts
#   wearing one number. ⭐ algebra/borne.sqlc settles it without touching this file: Σall = Σkept
#   + Σremoved, per layer, every run. It prints `3 held = 0 absorbed + 3 unserved` for each of the
#   four layers above, the vacuum as arithmetic rather than as an argument in a comment.
#   ⛔ A hand probe cannot say it: a `sed` that matches nothing reports the opposite in silence.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder summed against the slack it names, keyed by pm:Remainder/pm:absorber.
SELECT b.filing, b.layer, b.buffer, b.borne, s.mode AS slack_mode, s.unit AS slack_unit
FROM (
    SELECT p.filing, p.layer, a.buffer, sum(h.share_mode) AS borne
    FROM      (
        :compose(layers/pressed.sqlc)
    ) p
    JOIN      (
        :compose(layers/absorber.sqlc)
    ) a USING (filing, layer)
    JOIN      (
        :compose(entries/served_holders.sqlc)
    ) h USING (filing, layer)
    WHERE p.sign = 'interference'
    GROUP BY p.filing, p.layer, a.buffer
) b
JOIN (
    :compose(entries/slacks.sqlc)
) s USING (filing, layer, buffer)
WHERE s.mode IS NOT NULL
